Polymarket has run ahead of Kalshi by 300-900% depending on the category.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:16.240
Open interest on Polymarket hit $762.65 million early this month.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:23.040
Total value locked briefly cleared $400 million at the end of October on DeFi Lama figure

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.480
the report sites, and Dex volume has run about 30 percent above the slower summer months.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.180
A front-end exploit drained user wallets. Traders still came back for the midterm results,

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:40.179
and the platform kept most of its value locked and its trading volume. Yesterday, this Missouri

00:01:40.179 --> 00:01:45.419
fight was already in federal court. Today, Robinhood and Polymarket filed their own complaints

00:01:45.419 --> 00:01:51.179
against state officials, gambling insider reported, seeking to stop Missouri from treating sports

00:01:51.179 --> 00:01:57.219
event contracts as gambling the state can police. QCX LLC, which does business as

00:01:57.219 --> 00:02:02.119
Polly Market, US, put a 40-page complaint in the Eastern District of Missouri on

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:07.479
November 9th, rg.org reported from the docket. It names Attorney General

00:02:07.479 --> 00:02:12.039
Catherine Hanaway and five gaming commissioners. The council ledge Commodity

00:02:12.039 --> 00:02:16.799
Exchange Act preemption, and a commerce clause problem in rules that keep online

00:02:16.799 --> 00:02:22.479
licenses with in-state excursion boats, in-state pro teams, or operators acting for them,

00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:27.679
that put servers inside Missouri, and that require the better to be physically in the state.

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:33.559
Those allegations have not been tested. Robin Hood's complaint follows a November 6th warning

00:02:33.559 --> 00:02:38.359
from the solicitor general that officials would seek a compliance order within three days.

00:02:39.059 --> 00:02:42.439
Hanaway answered the same day with counterclaims against Novig,

00:02:42.439 --> 00:02:47.019
under the Federal Unlawful Internet Gambling Enforcement Act, the Missouri

00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:52.059
Merchandising Practices Act, and state public nuisance law. She wants payments

00:02:52.059 --> 00:02:56.659
tied to sports wagering blocked, restitution, and civil penalties of up to

00:02:56.659 --> 00:03:03.599
$1,000 per violation. Crypto.com's OG.com and Polly Market filed in Arkansas the

00:03:03.599 --> 00:03:08.279
same Monday, pointing at that state's November 4th suit against Kalshi as

00:03:08.279 --> 00:03:09.439
the threat in front of them.

00:03:10.139 --> 00:03:15.139
Attorney General Tim Griffin has called Kalshi a straightforward gambling platform and

00:03:15.139 --> 00:03:16.439
a pocket-sized bookie.

00:03:16.979 --> 00:03:22.079
Twenty-seven federally recognized tribes and thirteen tribal organizations filed an amicus

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:26.139
brief Monday in the Second Circuit on New York side against Kalshi.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:31.879
The Indian Gaming Association, the National Congress of American Indians, and the Seminole

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:33.619
Tribe of Florida are in that group.

00:03:33.619 --> 00:03:39.179
Their argument is that the Commodity Exchange Act does not override the Indian Gaming Regulatory

00:03:39.179 --> 00:03:44.239
Act, and that these contracts could cut into tribal sovereignty and existing compacts.

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:50.199
The brief follows ones from 37 state attorneys general, plus the District of Columbia and

00:03:50.199 --> 00:03:55.739
the Northern Mariana Islands, from the American Gaming Association, and from former CFTC

00:03:55.739 --> 00:04:00.339
Chair Gary Gensler, who argues federal law does not pre-empt the states here.

00:04:00.339 --> 00:04:02.959
The CFTC has backed Kalshi.

00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:09.795
Nevada Senator Catherine Cortez-Masto, answering Chairman Michael Selig's November 6 directive

00:04:09.795 --> 00:04:15.455
against geographic limits on federally regulated exchanges, accused him of encouraging operators

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:19.675
to ignore court rulings that restrict sports event contracts in some jurisdictions.

00:04:20.175 --> 00:04:24.515
She wrote that the move to undermine tribal and state sovereignty is intended to create

00:04:24.515 --> 00:04:26.215
profits for the president's family.

00:04:26.215 --> 00:04:32.435
11 public comments are in on the CFTC proposal that would write sports event contracts into

00:04:32.435 --> 00:04:37.115
the federal definition of a swap, and the deadline is November 18th.

00:04:37.155 --> 00:04:41.195
Major operators, state regulators, and tribal interests had not filed yet.

00:04:41.855 --> 00:04:46.715
The text would cover event contracts on sports, politics, cultural events, and weather

00:04:46.715 --> 00:04:48.475
under the Commodity Exchange Act.

00:04:49.075 --> 00:04:54.875
A companion interim final rule keeps casino-style products, including qualifying state-regulated

00:04:54.875 --> 00:05:01.475
sportsbook wagers outside the swap definition. A final rule would not, by itself, decide whether

00:05:01.475 --> 00:05:06.735
federal law overrides state gambling limits, or whether every sports contract can be listed.

00:05:07.395 --> 00:05:12.415
Several petitions, including one from New Jersey, ask the Supreme Court to take that fight,

00:05:12.935 --> 00:05:19.155
nearly all 11 comments favor federal oversight. One Utah trader cut off by Robin Hood from new

00:05:19.155 --> 00:05:25.015
sports, political, and cultural positions after legal developments in the state, wrote that Utah

00:05:25.015 --> 00:05:30.515
traders should not lose a federally regulated market because a state has redefined for its own

00:05:30.515 --> 00:05:37.595
purposes what a swap is. Another trader in these markets since 2021 wrote that there is no logical

00:05:37.595 --> 00:05:43.655
reason for a 500-leg combo on a federally regulated exchange, and asked for sports contracts

00:05:43.655 --> 00:05:49.655
limited to broader outcomes and a minimum age of 21. One of the 11 submissions explicitly

00:05:49.655 --> 00:05:56.009
asked the agency to withdraw the proposal. Coinbase, Kalshi, and Kraken parent Payward

00:05:56.009 --> 00:06:01.569
had applications to list U.S. stock perpetual futures deemed approved on November 2nd.

00:06:01.969 --> 00:06:08.249
Those three, with DRW holdings, jump trading, and paradigm, have now filed a letter in the Southern

00:06:08.249 --> 00:06:12.689
District of New York supporting the CFTC against the Capital Markets Alliance.

00:06:13.449 --> 00:06:19.309
CoinDesk and CryptoNews.net both have the filing. The Alliance, backed by firms including

00:06:19.309 --> 00:06:24.229
Cebo and Citadel Securities, says open-ended futures on individual stocks

00:06:24.229 --> 00:06:30.829
belong with the SEC, not the CFTC. Unlike a traditional future, a perpetual in this fight has

00:06:30.829 --> 00:06:37.489
no expiry date. A CFTC spokesperson, writing to CoinDesk when that suit landed on November 3rd,

00:06:37.489 --> 00:06:41.009
called the action troubling and said markets should be governed by law,

00:06:41.449 --> 00:06:44.429
not litigation campaigns intended to block innovation.

00:06:45.459 --> 00:06:49.599
The ninth circuit, KRXI reported, denied Calcia re-hearing,

00:06:49.879 --> 00:06:52.839
and a ban on popular contracts stays in place in Nevada.

00:06:53.619 --> 00:06:58.299
An intratribal lawsuit is complicating a Calcia agreement with a tribe in Oklahoma.

00:06:58.999 --> 00:07:03.899
KOSU reported, and gambling news reports that the Alabama Quasar tribe

00:07:03.899 --> 00:07:06.699
Deb has sued Kalshi over a pouquet-trade's deal.

