00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:26.621
A noise trader is someone whose order is not a clean read of the facts, and that is

00:09:26.621 --> 00:09:31.181
how it works in the papers that treat this flow as part of the price, not a leftover.

00:09:31.861 --> 00:09:36.521
In that model, governance improves liquidity only when the market also has noise traders

00:09:36.521 --> 00:09:38.401
the authors call semi-informed.

00:09:38.401 --> 00:09:42.421
The strength of the effect depends on how much those traders participate.

00:09:43.061 --> 00:09:47.181
Governance and that participation have what the model calls a synergistic effect.

00:09:47.701 --> 00:09:51.201
Pull the semi-informed flow out, and the liquidity channel disappears.

00:09:51.981 --> 00:09:54.001
The step underneath is the counterparty.

00:09:54.501 --> 00:09:58.401
Someone with a better signal can trade only if someone else will take the other side.

00:09:58.941 --> 00:10:03.521
If everyone waits on the same information, there is no trade, and the improvement never

00:10:03.521 --> 00:10:04.661
shows up as liquidity.

00:10:04.661 --> 00:10:11.241
This paper model stocks, not event contracts, the piece it isolates still travels, money

00:10:11.241 --> 00:10:14.961
that is uninformed or only partly informed is not only error.

00:10:15.541 --> 00:10:18.741
In this account, it is a condition for anyone else to trade at all.

00:10:19.341 --> 00:10:24.261
A 2015 study in the International Journal of Financial Management looks for that mix in

00:10:24.261 --> 00:10:25.181
Indian equities.

00:10:25.641 --> 00:10:31.441
The authors use daily trades plus intraday prices, volumes and trade times at one day and

00:10:31.441 --> 00:10:36.741
five-day intervals for the nifty 50 names listed on both the National Stock Exchange and

00:10:36.741 --> 00:10:42.481
the Bombay Stock Exchange, and market returns from the NSE, Nifty and the BSE Sensex.

00:10:43.061 --> 00:10:48.301
They ask whether return variation includes noise trader risk, and whether short run arbitrage

00:10:48.301 --> 00:10:51.441
by informed traders pushes them into long, short hedges.

00:10:52.021 --> 00:10:57.221
Noise they argue has a systematic piece and a firm specific piece, and both move through

00:10:57.221 --> 00:10:57.641
time.

00:10:57.641 --> 00:11:03.681
them. Those pieces include idiosyncratic shocks and noise shocks. At lags, a long short book

00:11:03.681 --> 00:11:08.581
across these markets can hedge the fundamental systematic shock, and the fundamental firm

00:11:08.581 --> 00:11:14.221
specific shock, and may peel the noise shock off them. Once the same stocks are held on

00:11:14.221 --> 00:11:19.441
long short horizons, that long short return is what exposes noise running across names.

00:11:20.201 --> 00:11:25.621
Set beside the same exercise two years earlier, the abstracts pattern is directional, not

00:11:25.621 --> 00:11:30.301
a published coefficient. Intraday returns from the one-day and five-day data

00:11:30.301 --> 00:11:36.241
impound significant noise. Daily returns show high exposure. Weekly returns show moderate

00:11:36.241 --> 00:11:41.581
exposure. In the Garch models, conditional volatility of those long short returns shows

00:11:41.581 --> 00:11:46.561
the time-varying idiosyncratic noise highly persistent when noise traders are present.

00:11:47.201 --> 00:11:51.881
During the trading day the study says, prices impound information and noise together.

00:11:51.881 --> 00:11:57.601
A 2016 paper in qualitative research in financial markets challenges the habit of calling

00:11:57.601 --> 00:12:00.181
every individual trader a dumb noise trader.

00:12:00.781 --> 00:12:05.381
Experience researchers and practitioners rated the math and verbal demands of investment

00:12:05.381 --> 00:12:07.021
tasks from earlier studies.

00:12:07.541 --> 00:12:13.161
On that rating, individual investors can do a number of complex cognitive actions, especially

00:12:13.161 --> 00:12:17.561
higher order verbal reasoning, and they look more limited where the math gets harder.

00:12:17.561 --> 00:12:22.361
the authors note that the math heavy tasks are the ones considered more relevant to

00:12:22.361 --> 00:12:27.121
performance. They also fence the result. The measure is indirect so they will not

00:12:27.121 --> 00:12:31.761
claim a definite score for retail competence. A direct test would be a lab

00:12:31.761 --> 00:12:36.201
experiment and they say that data was not available for the retail investors in

00:12:36.201 --> 00:12:41.021
view. 10 tasks is all they could analyze which limits statistical power and

00:12:41.021 --> 00:12:46.321
blocks a deeper deductive test. Their notes stay on disclosure, put key investor

00:12:46.321 --> 00:12:51.481
documents mostly in words, tell people what studies like these found, and offer online

00:12:51.481 --> 00:12:53.881
math practice built for individual investors.

00:12:54.301 --> 00:12:55.841
That is not a trading rule.

00:12:56.381 --> 00:13:00.781
The 2020 piece is a model, and its noise trader is semi-informed, not blank.

00:13:01.401 --> 00:13:06.781
The 2015 study finds noise that stays persistent inside the day in one equity market during

00:13:06.781 --> 00:13:07.381
a recovery.

00:13:07.861 --> 00:13:10.801
It does not size that effect on an event contract.

00:13:10.801 --> 00:13:16.821
The 2016 authors reject a blanket label, then mark how narrow their own rejection is.

00:13:17.241 --> 00:13:19.721
10 tasks, no direct performance test.

00:13:20.281 --> 00:13:24.481
What you can still do with a contract price is smaller than a slogan and more useful.

00:13:25.181 --> 00:13:30.581
A move can be information, or it can be the other side of an order that was never about the fact you are watching.

00:13:31.281 --> 00:13:35.481
Liquidity in the 2020 account is partly supplied by that second group.

00:13:36.181 --> 00:13:40.901
Persistence in the 2015 account means the noise need not be gone by the close.

00:13:41.461 --> 00:13:47.081
The 2016 assessment says the people in that flow are uneven, stronger on verbal reasoning

00:13:47.081 --> 00:13:51.401
than on the math performance is said to require, not uniformly lost.

00:13:51.921 --> 00:13:55.741
None of this names which side of a live contract is the informed side.

00:13:56.181 --> 00:14:01.121
A price is a trade and a trade needs a counterparty who may not share your reason for being there.

00:14:01.121 --> 00:14:06.571
Before we go, New Jersey's petition is among those asking the Supreme Court to take the

00:14:06.571 --> 00:14:10.731
question of whether federal law overrides state gambling limits on these contracts.

